Facts from other projects
-------------------------

- python-miio (github.com/rytilahti/python-miio, GPL-3.0): the miIO
  packet and the method sets of the legacy models the simulator answers;
  from v0.2.0 also the Roborock vacuum methods, the lumi gateway
  sub-device methods, the firmware update request and states, and the
  push scene layout; from v0.3.0 also the Roborock legacy extras
  (consumables, cleaning history, do-not-disturb, timers, sound, custom
  and carpet mode), miIO.config_router and the mDNS instance name (facts
  only; no code or data was taken).
- hass-xiaomi-miot (github.com/al-one/hass-xiaomi-miot, Apache-2.0),
  from v0.3.0: the translations path of the specification service and
  its answer's shape (facts only).
- Xiaomi-cloud-tokens-extractor
  (github.com/PiotrMachowski/Xiaomi-cloud-tokens-extractor; MIT,
  Copyright (c) 2020 Piotr Machowski): the Mi account endpoints the
  simulated account answers, from v0.2.0 with the captcha and
  identity-check steps (facts only).
- micloud (github.com/squachen/micloud; MIT, Copyright (c) 2020 Sammy
  Svensson): that sign-in may come as a form body and expects "result":
  "ok", and the older home/device_list (facts only, from running it).
- The Yeelight Inter-Operation Specification: that a Yeelight refuses
  changes while off.
- miot-spec.org: the format the simulated specification service serves.

Interop tests (interop/, a separate test-only module)
-----------------------------------------------------

interop/peer/Dockerfile downloads python-miio (GPL-3.0) at a fixed
commit and installs it, with its dependencies (micloud among them, MIT),
into a python:3.12.10-slim image at test time, to run its client;
nothing of python-miio or micloud is copied into this repository, and
neither is linked with this module. interop/peer/client.py is our own
script that calls them.

